Python App Dockerization on App Server 3
Problem: Create a Dockerfile under /python_app directory, build an image named nautilus/python-app, create a container named pythonapp_nautilus mapped to port 8096.

Solution:

bash
# Create Dockerfile
cd /python_app
cat > Dockerfile << 'EOF'
FROM python:3.11-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY src/requirements.txt .
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt
COPY src/ .
EXPOSE 6100
CMD ["python", "server.py"]
EOF

# Build the image
docker build -t nautilus/python-app .

# Run the container
docker run -d --name pythonapp_nautilus -p 8096:6100 nautilus/python-app

# Test
curl http://localhost:8096/
